@using DYS.Molargo.Domain.Enums
@using DYS.Molargo.Shared.Features.Diary.Services
@using DYS.Molargo.Shared.Features.Diary.ViewModels

@*
    The design's pre-booking checks column — what the front desk should know before
    committing the slot.

    Every panel here reads the record. Where the design promises something the app cannot
    yet know, the panel says so instead of showing a reassuring line nothing backs up:
    "FTA history — none · confirmed last 4 reminders" is worse than silence if nobody is
    tracking reminders.
*@

<div class="flex flex-col gap-3 px-6 py-5">
    <h6 class="m-0">Pre-booking checks</h6>

    @if (!Vm.HasPatient)
    {
        <div class="text-sm text-ink/55">
            Choose a patient and their alerts, lab work and account show here.
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-[13px]">

            @* ---- clashes ---- *@
            @if (Vm.Checks.Clashes.Count > 0)
            {
                @*
                    First, because these are the only checks about the slot rather than the
                    patient — and the ones the person filling the form can still fix.

                    Grouped by what the booking collides with. There used to be one heading
                    saying "Chair already booked", which was also the only check that ran,
                    so a clinician booked into two chairs at the same hour was reported as
                    nothing at all. They are separated because the fixes differ: a chair
                    clash moves chairs, a clinician clash cannot.
                *@
                @foreach (var group in Vm.Checks.Clashes.GroupBy(clash => clash.Kind))
                {
                    <div class="border-l-[3px] border-accent bg-accent-100 p-2.5 text-accent-800">
                        <strong>
                            @(group.Key == ClashKind.Chair
                                ? "Chair already booked"
                                : $"{Vm.ProviderName ?? "This clinician"} is already treating someone")
                        </strong> —
                        @foreach (var clash in group)
                        {
                            <span class="mr-2">
                                @clash.PatientName
                                @clash.StartLocal.ToString("HH\\:mm")
                                (@clash.Minutes min)
                            </span>
                        }

                        <div class="mt-1 text-[11px]">
                            @if (group.Key == ClashKind.Chair)
                            {
                                <text>
                                    This can still be saved — double-booking is sometimes
                                    deliberate — and the diary will draw the two side by side.
                                </text>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                @* Not refused, for the same reason, but it is the rarer
                                   and worse of the two: an assistant can prepare a second
                                   chair, a dentist cannot be in both at once. *@
                                <text>
                                    In another chair at the same time. Still saveable, but
                                    unlike a shared chair this one needs somebody to be in
                                    two places.
                                </text>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
            }

            @* ---- medical alerts ---- *@
            @if (Vm.Checks.Alerts.Count > 0)
            {
                <div class="border-l-[3px] border-accent bg-accent-100 p-2.5 text-accent-800">
                    <strong>Medical alerts</strong> —
                    @string.Join(" · ", Vm.Checks.Alerts.Select(alert => alert.Summary))

                    @foreach (var alert in Vm.Checks.Alerts.Where(a => a.Detail is { Length: > 0 }))
                    {
                        <div class="mt-1 text-[11px]">@alert.Summary: @alert.Detail</div>
                    }
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="bg-surface p-2.5">
                    <strong>Medical alerts</strong> — none recorded
                </div>
            }

            @* ---- lab work ---- *@
            <div class="bg-surface p-2.5">
                <strong>Lab work</strong> —
                @if (Vm.Checks.LabCases.Count == 0)
                {
                    @:nothing outstanding
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="mt-1 flex flex-col gap-1 text-[11px]">
                        @foreach (var labCase in Vm.Checks.LabCases)
                        {
                            <div class="@(labCase.Status == LabCaseStatus.Received ? "" : "text-accent-800")">
                                @labCase.Description —
                                @LabStatusLabel(labCase.Status)
                                @if (labCase.DueOn is { } due)
                                {
                                    @($", due {MolargoFormat.Date(due)}")
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>

                    @* Said explicitly: a fit booked before the lab work lands is a wasted
                       chair hour and a second trip for the patient. *@
                    <div class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-ink/55">
                        Only work marked received is safe to book a fit against.
                    </div>
                }
            </div>

            @* ---- account ---- *@
            <div class="bg-surface p-2.5">
                <strong>Account</strong> —
                @if (Vm.Checks.Balance == 0m)
                {
                    @:nothing owing
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="@PatientCss.BalanceCss(Vm.Checks.Balance)">
                        @MolargoFormat.Money(Vm.Checks.Balance) owing
                    </span>
                }
                <div class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-ink/55">
                    Payment plans are a billing feature and are not tracked yet, so a
                    balance here does not mean nothing has been arranged.
                </div>
            </div>

            @* ---- FTA history ---- *@
            <div class="bg-surface p-2.5">
                <strong>FTA history</strong> —
                @if (Vm.Checks.FailedToAttendCount == 0)
                {
                    @:no missed appointments
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="font-bold text-accent-800">
                        @Vm.Checks.FailedToAttendCount
                        missed @(Vm.Checks.FailedToAttendCount == 1 ? "appointment" : "appointments")
                    </span>
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <h6 class="mt-2 mb-0">Reminders</h6>
        <div class="bg-surface p-2.5 text-[13px] text-ink/55">
            @*
                The design states a cadence — "email + SMS 7d · two-way SMS 48h · SMS 2h".
                Still not repeated here. Both gateways send now, but nothing runs on a
                schedule, and a stated cadence would tell the front desk this patient will
                be reminded three times when they will be reminded never.
            *@
            No reminders are scheduled. A message goes out when somebody ticks a box on this
            form; nothing sends on a timetable, so confirm this appointment by phone if it
            matters.
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public AppointmentEditViewModel Vm { get; set; } = default!;

    private static string LabStatusLabel(LabCaseStatus status) => status switch
    {
        LabCaseStatus.Prepared => "not yet sent",
        LabCaseStatus.SentToLab => "at the lab",
        LabCaseStatus.InProduction => "in production",
        LabCaseStatus.Received => "received ✓",
        LabCaseStatus.Remake => "remake in progress",
        _ => status.ToString(),
    };
}
